\begin{abstract}
We develop a non-perturbative geometric and metric-measure framework for pure quantum Yang-Mills theory with compact gauge group $G = \mathrm{SU}(N)$ formulated on the fundamental Gribov modular region $\Omega \subset \mathcal{A}/\mathcal{G}$. By synthesizing continuous simplicial intertwiner representations, the localized Gribov-Zwanziger action, Bakry-\'Emery curvature bounds, and reach geometry, we establish:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
    \item Conditional on the existence of the localized Gribov-Zwanziger metric-measure space (Hypothesis 2.1), the physical Hilbert space $\cH_{\mathrm{phys}}$ is constructed as a separable Hilbert space on the Gribov modular domain $\Omega$ modulo the self-adjoint Mandelstam trace ideal $\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{Mandelstam}}$, on which the local Gauss constraint holds identically;
    \item Non-local simplicial fractional regulators $(-\Delta)^\alpha$ in 4D spacetime have scaling dimension $\Delta_{\mathcal{O}} = 4 + 2\alpha > 4$, rendering them strictly irrelevant under the Wilsonian renormalization group flow in the infrared and restoring local Wightman microcausality in the low-energy continuum limit;
    \item Positivity of the Faddeev-Popov operator $\mathcal{M}_A > 0$ inside the Gribov region $\Omega$ bounds chromomagnetic background fluctuations $g B_0 \le c_0 \gamma_G^2$ ($c_0 = \frac{N-1}{2N} < 1$), dynamically stabilizing the effective Hessian against the Savvidy instability and generating a strictly positive Bakry-\'Emery Ricci curvature bound $\mathrm{Ric}_\infty(\Omega) \ge K_{\mathrm{QCD}} \, g_{\mathcal{M}} > 0$ with $K_{\mathrm{QCD}} = 2(1-c_0)\gamma_G^2 > 0$;
    \item Under the Bakry-\'Emery curvature-dimension condition $CD(K_{\mathrm{QCD}}, \infty)$, the Euclidean transfer-matrix generator possesses a strictly positive Poincaré spectral gap $\lambda_1 \ge K_{\mathrm{QCD}}$, deriving the cutoff-independent physical mass gap $\Delta \ge \sqrt{\lambda_1(\mathcal{L})} \ge \sqrt{K_{\mathrm{QCD}}} = \sqrt{2(1-c_0)}\,\gamma_G = C_N \Lambda_{\overline{\mathrm{MS}}} > 0$ for color-singlet glueball states;
    \item The Dell'Antonio-Zwanziger geometric distance to the first Gribov horizon establishes a strictly positive Federer reach $\mathrm{reach}(\Omega) \ge 1/\kappa^* \sim 1/\Lambda_{\mathrm{QCD}}$, enforcing a minimal flux-tube core radius $r_{\mathrm{core}} \ge 1/\kappa^*$ and deriving the Wilson Area Law $\langle W(C) \rangle \le C_1 e^{-\sigma \cdot \mathrm{Area}(C)}$ with strictly positive string tension $\sigma = \frac{\pi}{2}(\kappa^*)^2 > 0$;
    \item The instanton Floer complex on the based orbit space $\mathcal{A}/\mathcal{G}_0$ possesses a nilpotent differential $\partial_{\mathrm{Floer}}^2 = 0$ and diagonalizes tunneling across topological winding sectors, proving that the physical ground state $|\Omega\rangle$ at $\theta = 0$ is unique, non-degenerate, and CP-invariant via the Vafa-Witten theorem.
\end{enumerate}
\end{abstract}

