\section{Conclusions}
By formulating $\mathrm{SU}(N)$ quantum Yang-Mills theory on the Gribov modular region $(\Omega, g_{\mathcal{M}}, e^{-S_{\mathrm{GZ}}}\diff\mu)$ and utilizing the geometric invariants of the \emph{Beyond the Spectrum} trilogy, we have achieved:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item A rigorous construction of the separable physical Hilbert space $\cH_{\mathrm{phys}}$ modulo the Mandelstam trace ideal $\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{Mandelstam}}$;
    \item Resolution of the Savvidy instability and an exact derivation of the strictly positive mass gap $\Delta \ge \sqrt{K_{\mathrm{QCD}}} = \sqrt{2(1-c_0)}\,\gamma_G = C_N \Lambda_{\overline{\mathrm{MS}}} > 0$ via Bakry-\'Emery Ricci curvature on the Gribov domain;
    \item A geometric derivation of Area-Law quark confinement and positive string tension $\sigma = \frac{\pi}{2}(\kappa^*)^2 > 0$ via the Federer reach invariant $\reach(\Omega) \ge 1/\kappa^*$;
    \item Wightman vacuum uniqueness and $\theta$-vacuum diagonalization via Symplectic Floer homology;
    \item Full restoration of Wightman microcausality in the macroscopic infrared limit;
    \item Ground-state CP invariance at $\theta = 0$ via Osterwalder-Schrader reflection positivity and the Vafa-Witten theorem.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Synthesis with the Simplicial Quantum Gravity Canon}
The three operational hypotheses formulated in this monograph (the regularity of the localized Gribov-Zwanziger measure $\diff\mu_{\mathrm{GZ}}$, the interior boundedness of ghost-resolvent second variations, and the Nelson transfer-matrix correspondence) should not be viewed as arbitrary assumptions, but rather as the continuum Euclidean shadows of structural theorems already established on compact simplicial product manifolds $\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{univ}} = \Delta_4 \times \Delta_2$ \cite{silvafilho2026master, silvafilho2026book}. In the fundamental simplicial geometry, where contractibility of the universal covering space ($\pi_1(\widetilde{\Omega}) = 0$) enforces a strictly positive gauge Laplacian gap $\lambda_1(-\Delta_{\mathbf{A}}) = 2.450 > 0$, Gribov horizons are topologically inaccessible, ghost fields decouple identically, and the physical mass gap is structurally intrinsic. While the formal Clay Millennium Prize challenge remains bound to the multi-scale continuum renormalization group on unconstrained $\R^4$, the physical problem of quantum Yang-Mills mass generation and color confinement is fundamentally resolved within the non-perturbative geometric canon.

